WEBVTT

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:17.380
Tristan Andizalder, re-toned by George Gibson.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:25.193
Copyright, Black Cat Publishing.

00:00:25.253 --> 00:00:34.395
Part one, the minstrel.

00:00:34.455 --> 00:00:43.017
One cold winter evening, King Arthur and his knights were sitting at the round table in the castle of Camelot.

00:00:43.077 --> 00:00:47.007
Suddenly, a tall young man came into the great hall.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:51.328
He had dark hair and dark, sad eyes.

00:00:51.388 --> 00:00:54.009
His clothes were old but clean.

00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:56.700
He had a harp under his arm.

00:00:56.759 --> 00:00:59.543
Welcome to Camelot, young man.

00:00:59.602 --> 00:01:00.996
Said King Arthur.

00:01:01.056 --> 00:01:02.578
Are you a minstrel?

00:01:02.637 --> 00:01:04.208
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:01:04.268 --> 00:01:04.819
I am.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:06.120
Said the young man.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.431
Where are you from?

00:01:07.491 --> 00:01:08.852
Asked King Arthur.

00:01:08.912 --> 00:01:10.353
I'm from Cornwall.

00:01:10.413 --> 00:01:11.734
Answered the minstrel.

00:01:11.794 --> 00:01:12.615
Well.

00:01:12.675 --> 00:01:13.896
Said King Arthur.

00:01:13.956 --> 00:01:16.538
We like minstrels and their stories.

00:01:16.598 --> 00:01:21.052
Tell us a good story about brave knights and lovely ladies.

00:01:21.112 --> 00:01:24.444
Do you know the story of Sir Tristan of Leones?

00:01:24.504 --> 00:01:26.056
Asked one of the knights.

00:01:26.116 --> 00:01:27.527
Yes, I do.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.902
Answered the minstrel.

00:01:28.962 --> 00:01:34.140
Sir Tristan is a brave knight, but his story is very sad.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.281
Sit down and tell us.

00:01:36.341 --> 00:01:37.682
Said King Arthur.

00:01:37.742 --> 00:01:42.715
Everyone in the hall was interested in the story of Sir Tristan of Lianess.

00:01:42.775 --> 00:01:47.938
The minstrel sat on a stall and started telling his story to the king and his knights.

00:01:47.998 --> 00:01:52.910
Sometimes he spoke and sometimes he sang and played his harp.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.852
This is the story he told.

00:01:55.912 --> 00:02:00.646
For many years there were wars between Cornwall and Ireland.

00:02:00.706 --> 00:02:05.620
The Irish often sailed across the sea to Cornwall and attacked it.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.824
There were terrible battles, and many people died.

00:02:09.884 --> 00:02:15.429
King Mark of Cornwall wanted peace, but the Irish did not.

00:02:15.489 --> 00:02:17.691
He did not know what to do.

00:02:17.751 --> 00:02:22.666
One day he asked his cousin, King Rivelin of Leonesse, for help.

00:02:22.726 --> 00:02:28.382
Help me fight the Irish, and you can marry my beautiful sister.

00:02:28.442 --> 00:02:30.793
Said King Mark to his cousin.

00:02:30.853 --> 00:02:33.224
The Irish and my enemies too.

00:02:33.284 --> 00:02:34.876
Said King Rivelin.

00:02:34.936 --> 00:02:36.546
I'll help you fight them.

00:02:36.606 --> 00:02:40.540
Together we can win, and I'll marry your beautiful sister.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:46.823
King Rivelin and King Mark fought together and won the war against the Irish.

00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:52.987
King Rivelin married King Mark's sister, and they returned to his castle in Leoness.

00:02:53.047 --> 00:02:57.169
They loved each other and were very happy together.

00:02:57.229 --> 00:03:00.662
But their happiness did not continue for long.

00:03:00.722 --> 00:03:05.064
A year later, King Rivelin was killed in battle.

00:03:05.124 --> 00:03:11.568
At the same time, the queen had a son, but she died soon after.

00:03:11.628 --> 00:03:15.940
Before dying, she called her servant, Ruel.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.412
Ruel, I'm dying.

00:03:18.472 --> 00:03:21.025
Said the young, beautiful queen.

00:03:21.085 --> 00:03:24.128
Take my child and call him Tristan.

00:03:24.188 --> 00:03:26.350
His name means sadness.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.392
It comes from the French word Trist.

00:03:29.452 --> 00:03:32.693
Look after him and love him like a son.

00:03:32.753 --> 00:03:37.786
And when he is a man, he must go and meet my brother, King Mark of Cornwall.

00:03:37.846 --> 00:03:39.687
He will help him.

00:03:39.747 --> 00:03:44.911
Ruel and his wife loved Little Tristan and they looked after him.

00:03:44.971 --> 00:03:47.974
He became a strong, brave boy.

00:03:48.034 --> 00:03:52.687
He learned to use a sword, a spear, and to ride a horse.

00:03:52.747 --> 00:03:57.120
He also learned to play the harp and speak other languages.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:04.636
When Tristan became a man, he left Leoness and went to Cornwall to meet his uncle, King Mark.

00:04:04.695 --> 00:04:08.478
The king lived in a big castle in Tintajal.

00:04:08.538 --> 00:04:14.622
Tristan entered the great hall of the castle and saw his uncle for the first time.

00:04:14.682 --> 00:04:18.895
Your Majesty, I'm your nephew Tristan from Leonesse.

00:04:18.955 --> 00:04:20.746
My nephew?

00:04:20.806 --> 00:04:24.267
Tristan, my sister's son.

00:04:24.327 --> 00:04:28.399
Said King Mark, looking at the tall young man.

00:04:28.459 --> 00:04:30.740
Welcome to Tintager.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.202
This is your new home.

00:04:33.262 --> 00:04:35.632
I'm very happy you're here.

00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:41.895
My knights and I will teach you many things and you'll become a great knight.

00:04:41.955 --> 00:04:45.516
Everyone welcomed Tristan to the castle.

00:04:45.576 --> 00:04:49.728
He was happy with his uncle, who loved him like a son.

00:04:49.788 --> 00:04:54.010
He became a famous knight and fought in many battles.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:59.332
The people of Cornwall knew about his great courage and liked him.

00:04:59.392 --> 00:05:06.305
But some of the knights and nobles were jealous of him because he was King Mark's favorite knight.

00:05:06.365 --> 00:05:11.800
One day, Sir Mohalt from Ireland came to Tintajal Castle.

00:05:11.859 --> 00:05:17.826
He was a gigantic man, with a dark face and strong hands.

00:05:17.886 --> 00:05:20.687
King Gurman of Eiland sent me here.

00:05:20.747 --> 00:05:22.898
He said in a loud voice.

00:05:22.958 --> 00:05:26.280
He wants a tribute from you, King Mark.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.961
A tribute?

00:05:28.021 --> 00:05:30.232
Said King Mark, surprised?

00:05:30.292 --> 00:05:32.224
Yes, a tribute.

00:05:32.284 --> 00:05:34.324
Said Samorholt.

00:05:34.384 --> 00:05:40.637
If you send a tribute, King Gurman won't attack Cornwall.

00:05:40.697 --> 00:05:43.018
What is the tribute?

00:05:43.078 --> 00:05:44.468
Asked King Mark.

00:05:44.528 --> 00:05:49.382
You must send him thirty noble boys, who will become his servants.

00:05:49.442 --> 00:05:50.262
What?

00:05:50.322 --> 00:05:51.814
Cried King Mark.

00:05:51.874 --> 00:05:54.526
Thirty of our noble boys.

00:05:54.585 --> 00:05:56.196
This is terrible.

00:05:56.256 --> 00:05:58.969
You must do what King Gorman wants.

00:05:59.029 --> 00:06:00.574
Set some more hold.

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:02.979
Or one of your knights can fight me.

00:06:03.039 --> 00:06:07.041
If your knight wins, you don't have to send a tribute to the king.

00:06:07.101 --> 00:06:09.162
But no one will fight me.

00:06:09.222 --> 00:06:14.276
I'm the strongest knight in the world, and everyone's afraid of me."

00:06:14.335 --> 00:06:19.388
Everyone was silent, but Tristan's face was red with anger.

00:06:19.408 --> 00:06:23.250
"'I will fight you, Sir Mohalt,' said Tristan.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.405
"'I'm not afraid of you.

00:06:25.465 --> 00:06:28.921
Everyone was surprised and looked at Tristan.

00:06:28.981 --> 00:06:30.302
No, Tristan.

00:06:30.362 --> 00:06:31.653
Don't fight him.

00:06:31.712 --> 00:06:33.804
He's too big and strong.

00:06:33.864 --> 00:06:35.115
Said King Mark.

00:06:35.175 --> 00:06:36.636
You can't win.

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:38.046
He'll kill you.

00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:39.748
No, Uncle Mark.

00:06:39.808 --> 00:06:41.038
Said Tristan.

00:06:41.098 --> 00:06:45.372
I'm a Knight of Cornwall and I must fight him.

00:06:45.432 --> 00:06:50.955
Sir Mohalt looked at the young man in front of him and started laughing.

00:06:51.015 --> 00:06:56.152
Tristan was much shorter and thinner than the Irish giant.

00:06:56.212 --> 00:07:00.586
I'll meet you in a week on a small island opposite the castle.

00:07:00.646 --> 00:07:02.197
Said Sir Moholt.

00:07:02.257 --> 00:07:05.348
Come alone, early in the morning.

00:07:05.408 --> 00:07:13.341
I'll be there, Sir Tristan, looking at Sir Moholt's cold eyes.

00:07:13.401 --> 00:07:20.054
Part two, Sir Moholt.

00:07:20.114 --> 00:07:25.772
A week later, Sir Moholt came to the island early in the morning.

00:07:25.832 --> 00:07:28.300
He pulled his boat onto the beach.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:33.294
Then Tristan came to the island, but he pushed his boat away.

00:07:33.354 --> 00:07:36.156
Why did you push your boat away?

00:07:36.216 --> 00:07:37.848
asked Sir Mohalt.

00:07:37.907 --> 00:07:41.110
You'll need it when you decide to run away from me.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:48.766
Tristan looked at him bravely and said, I won't run away because I'm not afraid of you.

00:07:48.826 --> 00:07:53.530
Remember, only one man will leave this island alive.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:58.223
Sir Mohalt laughed and raised his big sword.

00:07:58.283 --> 00:08:01.597
Tristan did the same and they started fighting.

00:08:01.656 --> 00:08:05.330
Tristan was young and light and he moved quickly.

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:10.696
Sir Mohalt was slow and heavy but he was very strong.

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:18.117
Tristan jumped here and there and soon Sir Mohalt was tired but he continued fighting.

00:08:18.176 --> 00:08:21.382
The fight went on for many hours.

00:08:21.442 --> 00:08:26.394
Suddenly, Sir Mohalt wounded Tristan's leg with his big sword.

00:08:26.454 --> 00:08:29.576
Test poison on my sword.

00:08:29.636 --> 00:08:31.878
Said Sir Mohalt, laughing.

00:08:31.938 --> 00:08:35.970
If you don't find someone to cure your wound, you'll be very ill.

00:08:36.031 --> 00:08:39.072
And only a few people in the world can cure it.

00:08:39.132 --> 00:08:43.766
Tristan was very angry and raised his heavy sword.

00:08:43.826 --> 00:08:48.302
He cut through Sir Mohalt's helmet and wounded his head.

00:08:48.362 --> 00:08:54.460
A small piece of Tristan's sword broke and remained in Samarholt's head.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:58.413
The Irish giant fell to the ground.

00:08:58.473 --> 00:09:00.774
He was almost dead.

00:09:00.834 --> 00:09:05.748
That evening, some of Samarholt's men came to the island.

00:09:05.808 --> 00:09:09.852
They were surprised to see him on the ground, wounded.

00:09:09.912 --> 00:09:15.792
They put him on their boat and sailed back to Ireland, where he died.

00:09:15.852 --> 00:09:23.614
His sister was the Queen of Ireland, and she was very sad because she loved her brother.

00:09:23.674 --> 00:09:32.870
She took the small piece of sword from Sir Mohalt's head and put it in a small blue box in her room.

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:37.794
One day I'll find the man who killed my brother, she thought.

00:09:37.853 --> 00:09:43.968
Tristan returned to Tintajal Castle, but his wound made him very ill.

00:09:44.028 --> 00:09:49.470
King Mark called the best doctors of Cornwall, but they could not help him.

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:54.082
Tristan must go to Ireland to cure his wound.

00:09:54.142 --> 00:09:55.762
Said an old doctor.

00:09:55.822 --> 00:09:59.114
Because the poison comes from there.

00:09:59.174 --> 00:10:05.287
The Queen of Ireland knows everything about poisons and herbs.

00:10:05.347 --> 00:10:07.508
She can help him.

00:10:07.568 --> 00:10:11.818
Then Tristan must go to Ireland immediately.

00:10:11.878 --> 00:10:13.078
Said King Mark.

00:10:13.138 --> 00:10:15.138
Get a ship ready.

00:10:15.198 --> 00:10:22.060
Tristan went to Ireland, dressed as a minstrel and called himself Tantris.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:26.501
He did not want anyone to know that he was Sir Tristan.

00:10:26.561 --> 00:10:32.500
He played the harp and sang beautifully and the Irish liked his songs.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:39.022
One day King Gurman heard about the minstrel and called him to his castle.

00:10:39.082 --> 00:10:46.446
King Gurman and his queen had only one child, a lovely daughter called Isolda.

00:10:46.506 --> 00:10:55.562
She was the most beautiful girl in the world with long blond hair, blue eyes and a lovely smile.

00:10:55.622 --> 00:10:58.628
Everyone talked about her beauty.

00:10:58.688 --> 00:11:05.005
The king wanted his alder to play the harp, but there were no good teachers in Ireland.

00:11:05.065 --> 00:11:09.677
Tantris entered the great hall of the castle with his harp.

00:11:09.737 --> 00:11:13.418
He walked slowly because his leg hurt.

00:11:13.478 --> 00:11:16.380
Are you the famous minstrel Tantris?

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.100
asked King German.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:21.772
Yes, I'm the minstrel, said Tristan.

00:11:21.832 --> 00:11:23.672
What's wrong with your leg?

00:11:23.732 --> 00:11:25.092
asked the king.

00:11:25.152 --> 00:11:29.672
I wounded it during a terrible battle, said Tristan.

00:11:29.732 --> 00:11:34.033
People say you play the harp beautifully, said King Gurman.

00:11:34.093 --> 00:11:36.743
Play something for me.

00:11:36.803 --> 00:11:43.495
Tristan played the harp and sang a lovely song, and the king was pleased.

00:11:43.555 --> 00:11:47.165
Can you teach my daughter, is all that to play the harp?

00:11:47.225 --> 00:11:48.736
Ask the king.

00:11:48.796 --> 00:11:52.956
Of course I can, said Tristan happily.

00:11:53.016 --> 00:11:55.811
Very well, said the king.

00:11:55.871 --> 00:12:01.977
The queen will cure your wound with her special herbs, and you will teach his older to play the harp.

00:12:02.037 --> 00:12:04.198
You can live here at the castle."

00:12:04.257 --> 00:12:07.959
Thank you, Your Majesty," said Tristan, smiling.

00:12:07.979 --> 00:12:13.800
"'I'm glad everyone thinks I'm a minstrel,' thought Tristan.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:19.424
Now my leg will get better, and I'll soon go back to Cornwall."

00:12:19.484 --> 00:12:23.266
Tristan's leg slowly got better.

00:12:23.326 --> 00:12:27.476
Every morning he taught his alder to play the harp and sing.

00:12:27.536 --> 00:12:32.107
His alder learned quickly and the king was very happy.

00:12:32.167 --> 00:12:41.780
During the harp lessons Tristan often thought, his alder is very beautiful.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:45.320
Part 3.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:55.724
The Dragon Tristan stayed in Ireland at King Gurman's Castle and taught his alder to play the harp and sing.

00:12:55.784 --> 00:13:00.937
He and his alder became good friends and often laughed and talked together.

00:13:00.957 --> 00:13:05.100
His alder became a good singer and harp player.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:10.274
She played the harp and sang songs for her parents and other nobles.

00:13:10.334 --> 00:13:14.387
After a year Tristan returned to Cornwall.

00:13:14.446 --> 00:13:24.538
King Mark was very happy to see his nephew Every day Tristan told his uncle about his older's great beauty.

00:13:24.598 --> 00:13:31.370
His older is the most beautiful girl in the world and she is gentle and kind.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:36.861
Her hair is the color of gold and her eyes are the color of the sea.

00:13:36.921 --> 00:13:41.892
She plays the harp well and sings with a sweet voice.

00:13:41.952 --> 00:13:52.716
King Mark listened to Tristan and said, Isalder is King Gurman's only daughter, and she is beautiful and kind.

00:13:52.776 --> 00:13:58.092
If I marry her, there will be peace between our two countries.

00:13:58.152 --> 00:14:04.772
The King's knights and nobles agreed with him, but there was one problem.

00:14:04.832 --> 00:14:10.960
We agree with you," said one noble, but how can you marry Princess Isalder?

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:16.234
The king and queen of Ireland hate us, because Sir Mohalt was killed here.

00:14:16.254 --> 00:14:17.646
He's right.

00:14:17.706 --> 00:14:19.596
Said another noble.

00:14:19.656 --> 00:14:27.002
King Mark was silent for a moment, and then said, I want to marry Isalder.

00:14:27.062 --> 00:14:33.096
I'll have the most beautiful wife in the world, and there will be peace between our countries.

00:14:33.156 --> 00:14:36.076
We must find a way."

00:14:36.136 --> 00:14:40.866
He looked at Tristan, but he didn't say anything.

00:14:40.926 --> 00:14:44.507
Tristan knew what his uncle wanted.

00:14:44.567 --> 00:14:50.158
Uncle Mark, said Tristan, I know this is a dangerous adventure.

00:14:50.218 --> 00:14:55.209
When the Queen of Ireland discovers who I am, she'll be very angry.

00:14:55.269 --> 00:15:00.767
She hates the knight who killed her brother Mohalt, but I'm not afraid.

00:15:00.826 --> 00:15:05.904
I'll bring Isola to you, Uncle Mark, and you can marry her.

00:15:05.964 --> 00:15:11.235
Your brave and loyal, Tristan, said King Mark.

00:15:11.295 --> 00:15:13.736
Be very careful.

00:15:13.796 --> 00:15:18.987
Tristan sailed to Ireland on a small ship with thirty men.

00:15:19.047 --> 00:15:22.648
They arrived in Ireland on a stormy night.

00:15:22.708 --> 00:15:26.618
I must think of a plan, thought Tristan.

00:15:26.678 --> 00:15:30.410
I must bring Isola to King Mark.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:36.302
At that time, a terrible green dragon lived in Ireland.

00:15:36.362 --> 00:15:41.964
It killed a lot of people and burned houses and trees with its fire.

00:15:42.024 --> 00:15:44.204
No one could kill it.

00:15:44.264 --> 00:15:49.046
King Gurman was worried and didn't know what to do.

00:15:49.106 --> 00:16:00.539
One day, he said to his nobles, The man who kills the terrible green dragon will marry my lovely daughter, Isolde.

00:16:00.599 --> 00:16:06.692
Everyone in Ireland was talking about this, and Tristan heard about it too.

00:16:06.752 --> 00:16:10.826
He was excited because he wanted to kill the dragon.

00:16:10.886 --> 00:16:16.512
He had a heavy sword, a long lance, and a big shield.

00:16:16.572 --> 00:16:23.503
He rode to the valley of the dragon and saw the dead bodies of other knights who tried to kill it.

00:16:23.563 --> 00:16:27.232
Suddenly Tristan saw the angry dragon.

00:16:27.292 --> 00:16:35.658
It was a terrible green monster with long white teeth, angry red eyes and a long tail.

00:16:35.718 --> 00:16:39.760
Fire and smoke came out of its mouth.

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:44.104
What an ugly creature thought Tristan.

00:16:44.164 --> 00:16:47.586
He attacked the dragon with his lance and sword.

00:16:47.646 --> 00:16:53.805
They fought for more than an hour and in the end Tristan killed it with his long lance.

00:16:53.865 --> 00:16:58.581
The dragon's last breath was hot and poisonous.

00:16:58.641 --> 00:17:01.832
Tristan soon felt very bad.

00:17:01.892 --> 00:17:06.172
He went to the dead dragon and opened its big mouth.

00:17:06.232 --> 00:17:11.333
Then he cut out its tongue and put it in his bag.

00:17:11.393 --> 00:17:16.244
This tongue will show that I killed the dragon, he thought.

00:17:16.304 --> 00:17:21.107
The poison made him ill and he fell to the ground.

00:17:21.167 --> 00:17:28.733
Later that day, one of the king's nobles called Seniscal came to the Valley of the Dragon.

00:17:28.793 --> 00:17:33.286
He liked his older very much and he wanted to marry her.

00:17:33.346 --> 00:17:37.058
But he was a coward and was afraid of the dragon.

00:17:37.118 --> 00:17:43.060
When Seniscal saw the dead dragon, he thought, this is wonderful.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.922
Someone already killed the dragon.

00:17:45.982 --> 00:17:50.750
I can tell the king I killed it and then I can marry his old.

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:56.710
But first, I must cut off the dead dragon's head to show the king.

00:17:56.770 --> 00:18:01.042
He cut off the head and took it to the king.

00:18:01.102 --> 00:18:05.424
Your Majesty, he said, I killed the green dragon.

00:18:05.484 --> 00:18:07.806
Look, here is its head.

00:18:07.866 --> 00:18:10.167
Now I can marry a daughter.

00:18:10.227 --> 00:18:12.058
Princess is old.

00:18:12.118 --> 00:18:17.631
The king knew Seniscale was a coward, and he did not believe him.

00:18:17.691 --> 00:18:21.324
But the head of the dragon was in front of him.

00:18:21.384 --> 00:18:27.009
When his older heard this, she started crying and could not stop.

00:18:27.069 --> 00:18:29.050
What's wrong, his older?

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:30.272
asked the queen.

00:18:30.332 --> 00:18:31.552
Oh, Martha.

